  "math_review": [
    "Walsh matrix H[i,j]=(-1)^popcount(i&j); seven sum/difference butterfly stages replace 128-term dense inner products. FP32 addition order changes and is separately numerically checked.",
    "Split/join gives compiler explicit low/high ownership. Total static instructions change only 93 to 92, but ds_bpermute falls 14 to 2, waits 9 to 3, and VGPRs 16 to 11; DPP/permlane replace most gather routing.",
    "Masks were not wholly eliminated: split formulation has 17 conditional masks vs gather13. Ten scalar nops remain. Do not characterize as universal opcode reduction.",
    "Both four-row variants use no LDS allocation, barriers or scratch. Eight-row gather uses 4096 bytes LDS and three barriers, so larger tiles were rejected.",
    "Post-commit ISA exactly retains 92 static instructions, two ds_bpermute and three waits. Resource descriptor VGPR11/SGPR17 differs from rounded profiler allocation VGPR12/SGPR32.",
    "No GEMM or base-kernel production code changed. Source-level matrix FLOP reduction is not a claim about executed MFMA counts."
  ],
